  "body": "Github tells me this is related: https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/issues/1577\r\n\r\nInstalled using pip on ubuntu, running 0.99rc4. `synctl stop` says it is stopping the homeserver, however the logs indicate that the server is still processing new requests with no indication of stopping. `synctl restart` has a similar problem in that it blocks for a long while until the server is manually stopped.\r\n\r\nAppears to not matter if workers are being used or not: the master process will always hang. Process requires `kill -9`. \r\n\r\nUsing python 3.",
